n:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:proxy","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds"],"statement":"Elevation, transfer, split, merge, proxy grant, revocation and retirement each need an explicit authority decision with an identifiable basis.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:authority-changes-need-decision"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"by default","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"the kinds may coincide in a lawful case","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:exception"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds"],"statement":"These may coincide in a lawful case and never collapse by default.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:authority-kinds-never-collapse"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:what-creates-no-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/ACTIVATION.md#admission"],"statement":"Only an admitted contract activates a step: no result, child completion, tool output, model response, shared actor or lateral handoff activates another step or authorises continuation by itself, and a profile that routes results names its instances of this rule.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:only-admitted-contract-activates"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P3 Identity. An object's identity is declared (authority, kind, value) and survives admissible change; a boundary is a claim with a proof obligation.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:requires","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments"],"statement":"P6 Justification and authority. Definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports a claim on a basis; authority permits or disposes within scope.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:proxy","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"may","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"literal":"where the governing identity and authority law permits it","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:permits","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds"],"statement":"Human authority may act directly, or through an explicitly admitted bounded proxy where the governing identity and authority law permits it; proxy identity and human-authority identity stay distinct (P6, P3).","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:proxy-identity-distinct"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:standing"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"must-not","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:force"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:vocabulary:operator:forbids","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds"],"statement":"None of the following mints, widens, transfers or reconstructs semantic, evaluation, operation or decision authority (P6, P3): - actor identity, an actor's capability, its tools or its access; - a name, label, display label, status label, role name, capability string, locator, file name or path; - declaring, naming, selecting, activating or executing a frame, or occupying a role; - implementation reachability, a reachable code path or an available operation; - the shape of evidence or of a payload, or the availability of evidence inside a frame; - a passing check, a successful step, a completed review or a count of any of them; - copying, interpreting, encoding, evaluating, transporting, projecting, compressing, importing or acquiring material; - drafting, admitting or retaining a work contract, beyond what its owner has admitted; - composition, delegation, adapters, wrappers and registries, which may restrict admitted authority or carry it faithfully, and never widen its scope, add a role, increase its cardinality or change its kind.","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:what-creates-no-authority"}],"closure":{"clauses":["urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:authority-changes-need-decision","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:authority-kinds-never-collapse","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:only-admitted-contract-activates","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p3","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:p6","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:proxy-identity-distinct","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:what-creates-no-authority"],"residuals":[],"symbols":["urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:authority","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:concept:proxy","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:consequence","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:standing:premise"]},"frame_indexes":[{"clause_refs":["urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:authority-changes-need-decision","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:authority-kinds-never-collapse","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:only-admitted-contract-activates","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:proxy-identity-distinct","urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:clause:what-creates-no-authority"],"frame_ref":"stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds","residual_refs":[],"scope":"Decide whether something grants authority: the kinds of authority, what creates none, the changes that need an explicit decision, and the proxy limit.","source_refs":["stdo-3://build_tenants/claude/standards/FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds"],"uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:i3:frame-index:authority-kinds"}],"frame_refs":["stdo-3://buil